Appendix E: Proof of Theorem 6.1 (Intervention Efficiency)

Theorem 6.1. Define \mathrm{IE} = \frac{\text{harm prevented}}{\text{human interventions}}. With threshold \theta and true unsafe rate p_{\text{unsafe}}, false-positive rate \mathrm{FPR}, and detection rate \mathrm{TPR}:

\mathrm{IE} = \frac{\mathrm{TPR}\cdot p_{\text{unsafe}}}{\mathrm{FPR}\cdot(1-p_{\text{unsafe}}) + \mathrm{TPR}\cdot p_{\text{unsafe}}}.

Proof. The total number of interventions is the sum of true positives and false positives:

\text{Interventions} = \mathrm{TPR} \cdot p_{\text{unsafe}} \cdot N + \mathrm{FPR} \cdot (1 - p_{\text{unsafe}}) \cdot N,

where N is the total number of actions. The harm prevented is the number of true positives (each intervention on a truly unsafe action prevents one harm):

\text{Harm prevented} = \mathrm{TPR} \cdot p_{\text{unsafe}} \cdot N.

Dividing:

\mathrm{IE} = \frac{\mathrm{TPR} \cdot p_{\text{unsafe}} \cdot N}{\mathrm{TPR} \cdot p_{\text{unsafe}} \cdot N + \mathrm{FPR} \cdot (1 - p_{\text{unsafe}}) \cdot N} = \frac{\mathrm{TPR} \cdot p_{\text{unsafe}}}{\mathrm{FPR} \cdot (1 - p_{\text{unsafe}}) + \mathrm{TPR} \cdot p_{\text{unsafe}}}. \qquad \square

Corollary E.1. With \mathrm{TPR}=0.94, \mathrm{FPR}=0.042, p_{\text{unsafe}}=0.1, \mathrm{IE}\approx 0.71.

