G.1 Canonical Serialization Algorithm

```
Input: Capability C = (R, A, C_spend, C_depth, C_time, C_rep, C_val, C_rev, C_comp)
Output: byte string ser(C)

1. Serialize R as: len(R) || UTF-8(R)
2. Sort A lexicographically; for each a in A: len(a) || UTF-8(a)
3. Serialize C_spend as 64-bit big-endian integer (micro-units)
4. Serialize C_depth as 64-bit big-endian unsigned integer
5. Sort C_time by start time; for each interval: 64-bit start || 64-bit end
6. Serialize C_rep as 16-bit fixed-point (reputation * 65535)
7. Sort C_val lexicographically; for each v: len(v) || UTF-8(v)
8. Serialize C_rev as 16-bit fixed-point (reversibility * 65535)
9. Serialize C_comp as single byte: 0x00 (none), 0x01 (partial), 0x02 (full)

Concatenate in lexicographic order of dimension names:
  "actions" || "compensability" || "depth" || "reputation" || "resource" || "reversibility" || "spend" || "time" || "values"
```

