I.2 Cgroup BPF Egress Firewall

```
// Cgroup BPF program attached to connect4/connect6 hooks
// Enforces per-session network allowlist

SEC("cgroup/connect4")
int egress_filter(struct bpf_sock_addr *ctx) {
    __u32 dst_ip = ctx->user_ip4;
    __u16 dst_port = ctx->user_port;
    
    // Look up destination in session allowlist
    struct allowlist_entry *entry = bpf_map_lookup_elem(&allowlist, &dst_ip);
    if (!entry || !(entry->allowed_ports & (1 << dst_port))) {
        return 0; // EPERM
    }
    return 1; // ALLOW
}
```

I.3 Formal Non-Bypassability Statement

Let \Sigma_{\text{all}} be the full syscall set and \Sigma_{\text{allowed}} \subseteq \Sigma_{\text{all}} be the allowed subset. The non-bypassability property is:

\text{Execute}(q) \;\Longrightarrow\; \text{seccomp}_{\text{hardened}}(q) \,\wedge\, \text{landlock}(q) \,\wedge\, \text{netfilter}(q) \,\wedge\, \text{ACP-admitted}(q)

Any q requiring \sigma \notin \Sigma_{\text{allowed}} is blocked at the kernel boundary with EPERM, before the ACP is consulted.

